title: Judicial Reform
new-page: true
is-card: true
on-arrival: judiciary_timer += 9; week_actions += 1
view-if: judiciary_timer = 0
card-image: img/portraits/XuQian.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

= Judicial Reform

The old Manchu-era systems of justice definitely needs reform. What should we do?

- @reform: Make substantial reforms in the judiciary.
- @minor_reform: Make smaller reforms in the judiciary.
- @as_is: Leave the judiciary alone first.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@reform
subtitle: -1 funds
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough funds.
choose-if: funds >= 1
on-arrival: funds -= 1; workers_kmt += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_kmt += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_kmt += 3*(1-dissent); judicial_reform += 2; pro_republic += 4*(1-dissent);

We have begun constructing a better, fairer and more efficient judicial system in Canton. 

@minor_reforms
on-arrival: workers_kmt += 1*(1-dissent); old_middle_kmt += 1*(1-dissent); new_middle_kmt += 1*(1-dissent); judicial_reform += 1; pro_republic += 2*(1-dissent);

We try to remove the most obviously biased and corrupt jurists, while leaving some of the old system intact, replacing more with new ones.

@as_is 
go-to: root
